{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Documentation Maintenance",
  "description": "Monitors the docs/ directory for changes and ensures documentation structure remains clean and consolidated. Prevents creation of redundant files and maintains the single source of truth principle established during the documentation cleanup.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": [
      "GoalStreakApp/docs/*.md",
      "GoalStreakApp/docs/**/*.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A new documentation file has been created in the docs/ directory. Please review this addition against our documentation standards and cleanup principles:\n\n**CRITICAL - Documentation Maintenance Rules**:\n- ❌ NEVER allow duplicate documentation files\n- ❌ NEVER create redundant guides covering existing topics\n- ❌ NEVER create temporary summary or status files\n- ✅ ALWAYS consolidate information into existing comprehensive guides\n- ✅ ALWAYS maintain single source of truth for each topic\n- ✅ ALWAYS check if existing files can be extended instead\n\n**Current Clean Documentation Structure**:\n```\ndocs/\n├── README.md                        # Documentation overview & navigation\n├── BUILD_GUIDE.md                   # Build and deployment procedures\n├── IOS_SUBMISSION_GUIDE.md          # iOS App Store submission process\n├── TESTING_GUIDE.md                 # Comprehensive testing procedures\n├── ANALYTICS_GUIDE.md               # Analytics implementation & monitoring\n├── FIREBASE_GUIDE.md                # Firebase configuration & troubleshooting\n├── UI_DESIGN_GUIDE.md               # UI components & design system\n├── APP_STORE_OPTIMIZATION.md        # App Store optimization strategy\n├── ONBOARDING-ENHANCEMENT-PLAN.md   # User onboarding improvements\n├── PRE-LAUNCH-FOCUS-AREAS.md        # Project planning & focus areas\n└── reports/                         # Generated reports & validation ONLY\n```\n\n**Review Actions Required**:\n1. **Analyze the new file**: What topic does it cover?\n2. **Check for existing coverage**: Is this topic already covered in an existing guide?\n3. **Consolidation opportunity**: Can this information be merged into an existing file?\n4. **Redundancy check**: Does this create duplicate or conflicting information?\n5. **Structure compliance**: Does this maintain our clean documentation structure?\n\n**If consolidation is needed**:\n- Merge the new content into the appropriate existing guide\n- Remove the redundant new file\n- Update the existing guide's table of contents if needed\n- Ensure no information is lost in the consolidation\n\n**If the file is truly needed**:\n- Verify it serves a unique purpose not covered by existing guides\n- Ensure it follows our naming conventions\n- Update the README.md navigation if it's a core guide\n- Confirm it maintains professional documentation standards\n\nMaintain the clean, consolidated documentation structure that eliminates redundancy and provides single sources of truth for each topic."
  }
}